  "scope": "T and R are native modal power fractions for the matched axial drive. Thickness contrasts subtract 200 nm from 100 nm and use 200 nm power as the relative baseline. Rim increments subtract 32 from 48 segments and use 32-segment power. The double difference subtracts the 32-segment thickness contrast from the 48-segment contrast and uses the signed 32-segment contrast as the relative baseline. Hole-wall segmentation and central remeshing change together at fixed nominal holes and leads. All five drives on each map passed the original equations and independent flux checks.",
